prove-bench: phil/prove against Z3, E and Vampire

	python3 -I tools/prove-bench/gen.py /tmp/bench 1
	emu -c1 -r$ROOT sh '#U*'$PWD/tools/prove-bench/run.inferno '#U*'$PWD '#U*/tmp/bench'
	EPROVER=... python3 -I tools/prove-bench/compare.py /tmp/bench path/to/vampire

gen.py writes 635 arguments in classes (see it); run.inferno runs prove
over them in InferNode, timing each, and writes each as TPTP (prove -t);
compare.py runs the others on the TPTP, 10 seconds an argument, and
tabulates.  The random 3-CNF classes (cnf*) are best run one emulator
each under a host timeout, as prove's search on them can run for minutes.

Results, 16 October 2026 (seed 1; a 4-core Linux container; Z3 5.3.0
through its Python API; E 3.5.1 built from source; Vampire built from
source, casc then casc_sat; prove under emu -c1, JIT, its cases searched
by clause learning):

