no disagreements

No prover contradicted another on any argument.  prove decides 634 of
the 635: every argument of the kinds people and models write (prop,
propm, mono, chains to 160), the random 3-CNF to 50 atoms, and 99 of
100 relational ones (Z3 54, E 90, Vampire 100); the one it leaves open
needs four individuals to refute.  It takes 10 to 30 ms on an argument
of paragraph or document size, its loading included (Z3 as a command
100 ms, E and Vampire 4 to 8), and well under a second on the large.

Before the clause-learning search (commit a9e81e1), prove's search was
plain backtracking: a chain of 160 took 14 seconds, and 11 of the 12
3-CNF problems of 30 atoms or more did not finish in 60.  On the 624 it
did finish, the new search's output is the old one's, byte for byte.

Modal and deontic (gen.py's s5 and kd classes; 150 each; prove -t
writes them by the standard translation, each atom holding at a world):

	class	n	valid	prove	Z3	E	Vampire	(right/undecided/wrong)
	s5	150	93	150/0/0	150/0/0	150/0/0	150/0/0
	kd	150	83	150/0/0	135/15/0	137/13/0	150/0/0

	seconds, median (max): s5 prove 0.014 (0.06), Z3 0.005, E 0.004,
	Vampire 0.007; kd prove 0.021 (80), Z3 0.015 (12), E 0.007 (10),
	Vampire 0.010 (2.9)

No disagreements.  (A first KD run, made while other benchmarks ran
beside it, had Z3, E and Vampire deciding 133, 82 and 84: they ran out
of their ten seconds under the load.  Run alone, Vampire decides all
150 as prove does, E 137, Z3 135.)  A first S5 run had prove out of memory on 17 (nested
operators copied at every world, at every level); S5 necessities and
possibilities are now each one atom, defined once, and the worst takes
0.06 seconds.  (That run also showed compare.py scoring problems prove
had not written; it now skips them.)

Against the dedicated modal provers (lwb.py): the Logics Workbench
benchmark for K (Balsiger, Heuerding and Schwendimann 2000), 18 classes
of 21 formulas, harder as they go; each prover climbs a class until it
fails twice, 10 seconds a formula; the score is the highest formula
decided.  KSP 0.1.6 (Nalon, resolution; its ijcar-2022 cord_mlple_K
configuration, with tcmalloc) and Spartacus 1.1 (Goetzmann, Kaminski and
Smolka, tableaux), built from the sources in
github.com/blorbb/modal-logic-benchmarks:

